  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Is Your Handheld Showerhead Underperforming?",
    "text": "Is Your Handheld Showerhead Underperforming?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Having a handheld showerhead that's not living up to its promise can be a real bummer. Maybe the spray is weak, or it's not reaching where you need it to, or perhaps it's even leaking. A lot of folks wonder if their unit is even compatible with their existing setup. Key questions often pop up around whether you need thread seal tape or special washers, or if the unit comes with all the bits like a diverter, bracket, and hose. The good news is, many common issues can be traced back to the installation. For example, overtightening connections can sometimes damage seals or even the fixture itself, leading to poor performance or leaks. Forgetting to clean the shower arm threads before installation can also mess with the seal. And sometimes, it's as simple as making sure you're using the right washers or thread tape specified for your particular model. If you're experiencing persistent low flow, ongoing leaks, or if your installation involves new diverter hardware or changes to your wall plumbing, that's when calling a pro like HH Remodeling LLC really makes sense. We can get it sorted out efficiently so you can enjoy your shower again.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
}